## Description

Rather than the mcp package monkeypatching the tool type to create it's own tool type use one unified tool type that has an optional `mcp` property that provides the tool with any mcp related features that come from being attached to an MCPServer class.

Tools used in an mcp server now have a different signature (but now the properties are also typed properly)

Tools can be easily written in both the mcp context and non mcp context now fully typed.

If added to an MCPServer it will use the `mcp` condition, otherwise it will use the other condition.

```
export const accountBalance = createTool({
  id: 'account-balance',
  description: 'Fetches the current account balance for a given account',
  inputSchema: z.object({
    accountId: z.string(),
  }),
  outputSchema: z.object({
    balance: z.number(),
  }),
  suspendSchema: z.object({
    message: z.string(),
  }),
  resumeSchema: z.object({
    confirm: z.boolean(),
  }),
  execute: async ({ context, mcp, suspend, resumeData}) => {
    const question = `Is it ok to fetch the account balance for account ${context.accountId}?`;
    
    if (mcp) {
      const result = await mcp.elicitation.sendRequest({
        message: question,
        requestedSchema: {
          type: 'object',
          properties: {
            confirm: { type: 'boolean' },
          },
          required: ['confirm'],
        }
      });
      if (result.action === 'accept') {
        return {
          balance: getAccountBalance(context.accountId),
        };
      } else if (result.action === 'decline') {
        return 'User declined to provide account balance';
      } else {
        return 'User cancelled account balance request';
      }
    } else {
      if (!resumeData) {
        return await suspend?.({
          message: question,
        });
      }
      if (!resumeData.confirm) {
        return 'User declined to fetch the account balance';
      }
      return {
        balance: getAccountBalance(context.accountId),
      };
    }
  },
});

```
